-- title:
--   Norms detect σ-twisted conjugacy of diagonal matrices in GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of fields and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $t,t' \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be matrices whose off-diagonal entries vanish, i.e. the $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries of each are $0$. Write $\sigma$ also for the entrywise action on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ induced by $\sigma$ viewed as a ring homomorphism $L \to L$, and set $N = \mathrm{Algebra.norm}\,K$ for the norm of $L$ over $K$. The conclusion is the conjunction of three equivalences. First, there exists $b \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $(1,0)$ entry $0$ (i.e. upper triangular) and $t' = b^{-1} t \,\sigma(b)$ if and only if $N(t'_{00}) = N(t_{00})$ and $N(t'_{11}) = N(t_{11})$. Secondly, the same numerical condition is equivalent to the existence of such a conjugator $a$ that is itself diagonal (both off-diagonal entries $0$). Thirdly, there exists an arbitrary $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $t' = g^{-1} t\, \sigma(g)$ if and only if either $N(t'_{00}) = N(t_{00})$ and $N(t'_{11}) = N(t_{11})$, or $N(t'_{00}) = N(t_{11})$ and $N(t'_{11}) = N(t_{00})$.
--
--   This is the classification of $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy classes of diagonal elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension: inside the Borel or the diagonal torus the invariant is the ordered pair of norms of the diagonal entries, while in the full group only the unordered pair is an invariant. It is used in the description of twisted stabilisers and in the decomposition of twisted conjugacy classes meeting the set of matrices with vanishing lower-left entry.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LT_TwistedNorm_exists_eq_inv_mul_mul_map_iff_norm_eq_of_diagonal.lean

